}-0\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,0\\,|=0\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268948 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0272b8d6-8400-5a6d-b51d-fc6ca84bd166" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Parallelogram Spanned by Two Parallel Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "094d5851-7aa6-53e8-8ba4-a2529411785d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268950} {:answer/id #uuid "90306f28-f1d2-5622-bfd0-6d6380e61ef3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268951} {:answer/id #uuid "0484dbf2-9846-5ef3-9c44-acdd5378063f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268952} {:answer/id #uuid "6f3bf6a7-3708-5c18-9721-6fe778af5c99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268953} {:answer/id #uuid "b690d5b6-7ccb-53dc-9b90-fb6c02ddf6a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b690d5b6-7ccb-53dc-9b90-fb6c02ddf6a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268954} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a4802a3-06aa-5a6f-8b8d-5043fc04882b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268949}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "821dcb20-0f05-5eb1-bd02-f59fc0e38b8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-69943" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]$ and $\\text{v}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}-6\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =2-2 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,0\\,|=0\n$$"}]}
